    "bodySha256": "df53b35e84ceaf3da3b44e452e1e6cf8d1010ff56667a6909c2f81b8af71273d",
    "body": "# omp-spec-kit v1.0.0\n\n## Included changes\n\n- Promotes the bounded 10-tool MCP surface to the stable major release: 9 read-only tools and one transactional `spec_patch` authoring tool.\n- Preserves bounded entity, graph, document, evidence, and Markdown queries with pagination, projections, cursors, and traversal limits.\n- Verifies the complete semantic tool-E2E matrix against the built server and the exact release archive launcher.\n\n## Verified release\n\n- Candidate digest: `d0fd5ea79fd41818042cd9f301dae76a1651426fb509701aa71bc36dc419714f`\n- Package tree digest: `fbe97bcc4d308d7148e716710641bf47d837de52f0b1231755c09ea3c920af1e`\n- Archive SHA-256: `af3449ec1d61faf0d934a1fbb1baa35912166beae9c82b4b8db79af97d27c63c`\n- Peeled tag commit: `13a1fcaf3dd886c7bfe6c2250904824ab2e7343f`\n- OMP runtime: `18.0.11`\n- Distribution evidence: lifecycle producers, Docker BDD, manager discovery, and nine closed MRI receipts.\n\nInstall or upgrade at project scope, reload plugin metadata, then start a fresh OMP session before invoking MCP tools.\n"
